Moved by Cr MacRae, seconded by Cr Langer

That in accordance with Part 4 of the Town of Cambridge Town Planning Scheme No. 1, Council APPROVES the application for a new two storey dwelling submitted by Artique Building Pty. Ltd. at Lot 1355 (No. 13) Kilkenny Road, Floreat as shown on the plans submitted 23 March 2009, subject to the following conditions:-

(i) the surface finish of boundary walls facing adjacent neighbours being rendered, painted or face brickwork to the satisfaction of the Town;

(ii) any existing crossovers not included as part of the proposed development on the approved plan being closed and the kerb and verge reinstated;

(iii) the retaining wall to the rear and the eastern boundaries being built to a height of RL17.80;

(iv) the crossover being amended to ensure a minimum 1.0 metre setback from the existing verge tree.

That:- 

(i) the establishment of a Treescape Advisory Committee be approved by an ABSOLUTE MAJORITY; 

(ii) the Terms of Reference for the Treescape Advisory Committee, as attached to and forming part of the Notice Paper, be adopted; 

(iii) Councillors Grinceri (Coast Ward) and MacRae (Wembley Ward) be nominated as the two Elected Members on the Advisory Committee; 

(iv) expressions of interest from residents/ratepayers wishing to be considered for the four community representative positions on the Advisory Committee be sought; 

(v) the ongoing need for the Advisory Committee be reviewed by the Administration no later than June 2009 and a report be submitted to Council.

Moved by Cr Berry, seconded by Cr Bradley

That:

(i) the report detailing the options for consideration for addressing speed and volume of traffic in Pandora Drive be received;

(ii) the development of the intersection of Empire Avenue / Durston Road be reviewed, in conjunction with the City of Stirling and the adjacent residents, and a proposal be submitted for Council consideration;

(iii) origin/destination surveys be completed on Pandora Drive traffic for consideration when evaluating further traffic management options;

(iv) the Administration be requested to evaluate traffic treatment options for Pandora Drive for presentation to Council and subsequent canvassing with residents.

Moved by Mayor Mack, seconded by Cr Le Page

